            <ArticleTitle>Evaluation and treatment of chronic ankle pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>311-21</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The evaluation and treatment of chronic ankle pain presents a challenge to the orthopaedic surgeon. A detailed history helps to determine causative factors resulting from earlier trauma or surgery. A careful physical examination and radiographic studies also are helpful in making an accurate diagnosis, which is the basis for choosing a specific and effective treatment regimen.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
